From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:45:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Link libfastjson with libm

json_object.c uses modf(), which is provided by libm. On glibc targets,
modf() is an IFUNC symbol, so libfastjson must carry its own direct
DT_NEEDED entry for libm instead of relying on another object to load it.

Without the direct dependency, rsyslogd can fail at startup with:

  Relink `/usr/lib64/libfastjson.so.4' with `/lib64/libm.so.6' for IFUNC symbol `modf'

Link libfastjson with libm explicitly.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 Makefile.am | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
index 28b1f85..95bb47a 100644
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ libfastjson_la_LDFLAGS = \
 	-export-symbols-regex '^fjson_.*' \
 	-no-undefined \
 	@JSON_BSYMBOLIC_LDFLAGS@
-libfastjson_la_LIBADD = libfastjson-internal.la
+libfastjson_la_LIBADD = libfastjson-internal.la -lm
 
 libfastjson_la_SOURCES = \
 	json_version.c \
